            <ArticleTitle>Effect of Leptin Administration on Circulating Apolipoprotein CIII levels in Patients With Lipodystrophy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1790-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1210/jc.2015-3891</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients with lipodystrophy had elevated apolipoprotein CIII (apoCIII) compared to healthy controls. ApoCIII did not change with leptin treatment despite significant reductions in serum triglyceride.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
